--- !u!114 &2850763914463123216
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 6636933741198875702}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f4688fdb7df04437aeb418b961361dc5, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.TextMeshPro::TMPro.TextMeshProUGUI
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "\"My dearest Minh,\n\nIf you are reading this, it means you\u2019ve finally
    come back to our park. I know how hard it has been for you to look at this bench
    without feeling the weight of that sunset.\n\nYou\u2019ve always had a way of
    capturing the world through your lens, but I feared you were using that camera
    to hide from the world rather than see it. Please, don't let that one moment\u2014the
    moment the light left my eyes\u2014be the only frame you keep in your heart.\n\nYou
    blame yourself for not being enough, for being 'broken' or 'depressed,' as you
    call it. But Minh, even a cracked lens can capture a beautiful sunset. The shadows
    you've been running from aren't there to swallow you; they are just part of the
    picture.\n\nForgive yourself for being human. Put the camera down for a moment,
    take a breath, and look at the sky. It's time to stop living in the Labyrinth
    of what was, and start seeing the light of what is.\n\nI am still here, in every
    golden ray and every rustle of the leaves. I love you, always.\n\n\u2014 Grandma\"\n\n\"My
    dearest Minh,\n\nIf you are reading this, it means you\u2019ve finally come back
    to our park. I know how hard it has been for you to look at this bench without
    feeling the weight of that sunset.\n\nYou\u2019ve always had a way of capturing
    the world through your lens, but I feared you were using that camera to hide
    from the world rather than see it. Please, don't let that one moment\u2014the
    moment the light left my eyes\u2014be the only frame you keep in your heart.\n\nYou
    blame yourself for not being enough, for being 'broken' or 'depressed,' as you
    call it. But Minh, even a cracked lens can capture a beautiful sunset. The shadows
    you've been running from aren't there to swallow you; they are just part of the
    picture.\n\nForgive yourself for being human. Put the camera down for a moment,
    take a breath, and look at the sky. It's time to stop living in the Labyrinth
    of what was, and start seeing the light of what is.\n\nI am still here, in every
    golden ray and every rustle of the leaves. I love you, always.\n\n\u2014 Grandma\""
